### Team Management API Tests
### Base URL
@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080
@contentType = application/json

### Variables - Update these with real values
@teamId = 
@userId = 
@invitationToken = 
@invalidToken = 
@notFoundTeamId = 

###
### List All Teams for Current User
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/teams
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

###
### Create a New Team
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/teams
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "name": "Family Team",
  "description": "Our family household team for managing tasks"
}

###
### Create a Team - Minimal (description optional)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/teams
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "name": "Kitchen Crew"
}

###
### Create a Team - Validation Error (name too short)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/teams
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "name": "",
  "description": "This should fail validation"
}

###
### Update Team (replace {{teamId}} with actual UUID)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/teams/{{teamId}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "name": "Updated Family Team",
  "description": "Updated description for our family team"
}

###
### Update Team - Name Only
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/teams/{{teamId}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "name": "New Team Name"
}

###
### Get Team Members (replace {{teamId}} with actual UUID)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/teams/{{teamId}}/members
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

###
### Invite User to Team as Member (replace {{teamId}} with actual UUID)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/teams/{{teamId}}/invite
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "member@example.com",
  "role": "member"
}

###
### Invite User to Team as Admin (replace {{teamId}} with actual UUID)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/teams/{{teamId}}/invite
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "admin@example.com",
  "role": "admin"
}

###
### Invite User - Validation Error (invalid email)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/teams/{{teamId}}/invite
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "invalid-email",
  "role": "member"
}

###
### Invite User - Validation Error (invalid role)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/teams/{{teamId}}/invite
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "user@example.com",
  "role": "invalid-role"
}

###
### Remove Member from Team (replace {{teamId}} and {{userId}} with actual UUIDs)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/teams/{{teamId}}/members/{{userId}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

###
### Get My Pending Invitations
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/teams/invitations
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

###
### Accept Team Invitation (replace {{invitationToken}} with actual token)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/teams/invitations/{{invitationToken}}/accept
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

###
### Accept Team Invitation - Invalid Token (should return error)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/teams/invitations/{{invalidToken}}/accept
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

###
### Team Not Found (should return 404)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/teams/{{notFoundTeamId}}/members
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

###
### Unauthorized Action - Non-admin trying to invite (should return 403/401)
# First login as a non-admin user, then try to invite
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/teams/{{teamId}}/invite
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "newuser@example.com",
  "role": "member"
}

###
### Complete Team Creation and Invitation Flow Example
### 1. Create a team
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/teams
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "name": "Test Team",
  "description": "Team created for testing the complete flow"
}

### 2. Save the teamId from the response above and use it below
### 3. Invite a member
# POST {{baseUrl}}/api/teams/{{teamId}}/invite
# {
#   "email": "testmember@example.com",
#   "role": "member"
# }

### 4. Check invitations (login as the invited user)
# GET {{baseUrl}}/api/teams/invitations

### 5. Accept invitation (use token from step 4)
# POST {{baseUrl}}/api/teams/invitations/{{invitationToken}}/accept

### 6. Verify team members
# GET {{baseUrl}}/api/teams/{{teamId}}/members
